.TH SYSBLINK 1 "2026" "sysblink 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysblink \- show system metrics on leds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysblink.py
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B preview.py
.I patch
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysblink
builds small c daemons that show cpu, memory, swap, disk io, network
traffic, temperature, battery charge or load average on sysfs leds and
registers them with the detected init system. a patch is one c file in the
patches directory, the installer inserts it into the engine template and
compiles the result. the patch contract is described in docs/patches.md.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR "\-\-lang " en|ru
interface language
.TP
.B \-\-list_leds
list writable leds and exit
.TP
.B \-\-list_patches
list available patches and exit
.TP
.B \-\-list_inits
list init backends, the detected one is marked
.TP
.BI "\-\-build " led,patch
build a daemon for one led or a comma separated list of leds and one patch
.TP
.BI "\-\-hz " n
update frequency in hertz, 1 to 100
.TP
.B \-\-install
register the built daemon with the init system
.TP
.BI "\-\-init " backend
use this backend instead of the detected one: systemd, openrc, runit, s6,
sysvinit or none
.TP
.B \-\-remove
remove one installed service
.TP
.B \-\-remove_all
remove every installed service
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit
.PP
.B preview.py
runs a patch against a fake led and draws the level in the terminal,
.B \-\-once
prints one bar and exits, q quits the live view.
.SH CONFIG
defaults are read from sysblink.conf next to the installer: lang, hz, init,
led, patch, disk and iface. disk pins the watched block device and iface
pins the counted network interface, empty means the patch default. a flag
on the command line beats the file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/leds/*
leds the daemon writes to, the trigger file is switched to none at startup
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/sysblink_*
installed daemon binaries
.TP
.I /var/lib/sysblink/build
build directory of the packaged installer
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the led cannot be opened or writes keep failing, so a
supervising init system restarts the daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/patches.md, docs/patches.ru.md
